@startuml
title Matrix Login Entitlement — Example Flow
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #334155
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFF7D6
  DiamondBorderColor #A16207
}

start
:Browser or Matrix client starts MAS upstream OIDC login;
:MAS redirects to Keycloak;
:Run the MAS client's dedicated Keycloak Browser flow;
note right
  The flow requires the existing Browser
  Methods subflow, preserving cookie, IdP,
  password and MFA behavior. It then runs
  a direct conditional missing-role branch.
  The v2 flow has no empty required wrapper.

  Keycloak account can remain enabled when
  the role is absent. Entitlement is checked
  for Matrix authentication; it need not disable
  unrelated Keycloak applications.

  Verify flow binding, role mapping, and denial
  behavior in each deployment.
end note
:Complete existing browser methods (SSO cookie, IdP, password, MFA as configured);
if (Effective matrix-access realm role absent?) then (yes)
  :Conditional missing-role subflow runs;
  :Deny Access authenticator rejects;
  :No OIDC success response;
  stop
else (no)
  :Conditional subflow is skipped;
  :Continue OIDC response to MAS;
  :MAS completes Matrix authentication;
  :Issue Matrix session;
  stop
endif

@enduml
